config SAMPLE_HARDEN
	tristate "Buggy KCOV/KASAN hardening demo drivers"
	depends on KCOV && m
	help
	  Build three deliberately buggy misc-device drivers used by the
	  "KCOV + libFuzzer/FuzzTest + KASAN" hands-on hardening tutorial:

	    harden_local  - parses a zero-copy shared page in syscall context
	                    (local KCOV coverage).
	    harden_remote - parses the same page on a workqueue kthread
	                    (remote KCOV coverage, KCOV_REMOTE_ENABLE).

	    harden_ledger - a per-file memory quota whose accounting drifts
	                    after ALLOC/RESIZE/FREE (a logic bug KASAN cannot
	                    see; found by a FuzzTest model-based property).

	  The first two contain a write-side out-of-bounds bug behind an
	  under-covered branch, intended to be found by the userspace libFuzzer
	  harnesses in tools/harden/sample/ or the FuzzTest harnesses in
	  tools/harden/fuzztest/. Do NOT enable on a production kernel.

	  If unsure, say N.
